  "question": {
    "text": "Let $x=x(y)$ be the solution of the differential equation $y=\\left(x-y \\frac{\\mathrm{~d} x}{\\mathrm{~d} y}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right), y\\gt0$ and $x(1)=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$. Then $\\cos (x(2))$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5HUaP",
      "text": "$1-2\\left(\\log _e 2\\right)^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "sA8ff",
      "text": "$1-2\\left(\\log _{\\mathrm{e}} 2\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "P3ANZ",
      "text": "$2\\left(\\log _e 2\\right)-1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ct1ON",
      "text": "$2\\left(\\log _e 2\\right)^2-1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & y d y=(x d y-y d x) \\sin \\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right) \\\\ & \\frac{d y}{y}=\\left(\\frac{x d y-y d x}{y^2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right) \\\\ & \\frac{d y}{y}=\\sin \\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right) d\\left(-\\frac{x}{y}\\right) \\\\ & \\rightarrow \\ell n y=\\cos \\frac{x}{y}+C\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & x(1)=\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\Rightarrow 0=\\cos \\frac{\\pi}{2}+C \\Rightarrow C=0 \\\\ & \\text { lny }=\\cos \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ & \\text { but } y=2 \\Rightarrow \\cos \\frac{x}{2}=\\ell n 2 \\\\ & \\cos x=2 \\cos ^2 \\frac{x}{2}-1 \\\\ & =2(\\ln 2)^2-1\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
